# ME8 — UI chrome title case (whole product)

**Disc:** `docs/MOB-DISC-UI-COPY-SENTENCE-CASE-V1.md`  
**APPLY done:** `UI-COPY-SENTENCE-CASE-V1`

## Locked voice (new pages, new tabs, new labels)

| Kind | Rule | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Heading / tab / **field label** | **Each principal word** capital — not first-word-only | `New Username` · `Account Type` · `Operator Portal URL` |
| Small joiners | Stay lower | `Evidence and Docking` · `Route and GPS` · `Help and About` |
| Acronyms | Stay shouted | IP, URL, FTP, GPS, SSO, BWC, SOS, IPv4, HTTPS, LAN, USB, OIDC |
| After a leading acronym | Next word capital | `IP Assignment` · `FTP Host (for docks)` |
| Ampersand **`&`** | **Do not use** in tabs/headings | `Route and GPS` not `Route & GPS` |
| Lazy **Config** | Ban in chrome — use **Configuration** or Settings | `Server Configuration` not `Server Config` |

**Not chrome:** officer-typed data, case IDs, logs, toast sentence bodies, manuals. Those stay normal sentences.

## Agent rules for new UI

1. **Copy only** — edit `public/locales/en.json` + matching HTML `data-i18n` fallbacks. No JS logic, no `id`/`name`/handler changes.
2. **No layout MOBs bundled** — do not change boxes, grids, padding, or CSS width unless a separate named APPLY says so.
3. **CSS** — chrome titles/labels use `text-transform: none` (see `settings-theme-unify.css`). Never add `uppercase` on h3/h4/field labels — that shouts over title-case strings.
4. **If a string change makes text overflow or clip a box** — stop; leave copy as-is and tell the operator which label/page visually broke.
5. **Whole-UI grep** only when user names a MOB or asks for a sweep. Default: fix the keys you touch on that page.

## Where strings live

- Primary: `public/locales/en.json`
- Fallback: same text on `data-i18n="…"` nodes in HTML
- Settings titles: `#server-setup-panel h4` already `text-transform: none` in unify CSS
